Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:23:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] XHTTP: Cover flow governor credit in both ramp states, time
 SETTINGS frames the clock can tell

Each credit test runs with the stream speeding up and no longer; connection credit comes before the stream's and after, alone for a request whose body has ended, and follows a cap that opens. The SETTINGS cost test doubles its number of frames until two hundred streams take two milliseconds instead of skipping where they read as zero.
---
 .../internet/splithttp/h2flow_credit_test.go  | 255 +++++++++++++-----
 .../splithttp/h2flow_sendwindow_test.go       |  31 ++-
 2 files changed, 211 insertions(+), 75 deletions(-)

diff --git a/transport/internet/splithttp/h2flow_credit_test.go b/transport/internet/splithttp/h2flow_credit_test.go
index 4a38fbb10..e417c9e43 100644
--- a/transport/internet/splithttp/h2flow_credit_test.go
+++ b/transport/internet/splithttp/h2flow_credit_test.go
@@ -29,44 +29,173 @@ func windowUpdates(t *testing.T, b []byte, count map[uint32]int, sum map[uint32]
 	}
